  "id": "COMPOUND:21337 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Neridienone A appears to have a shared target, SNU-387, with multiple compounds, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving SNU-387. The evidence indicates that SNU-387 is a target of Isoamyl isobutyrate, Tetraethylammonium, and Thelephantin K, all of which have a common relationship with DNA polymerase iota. This suggests that DNA polymerase iota may be a downstream target of these compounds, potentially through a common pathway or mechanism. The integration of these findings implies that Neridienone A may interact with SNU-387, which in turn interacts with these compounds, ultimately leading to the inhibition of DNA polymerase iota. The consistent presence of SNU-387 as a target across different compounds supports a possible role in the mechanism of action of Neridienone A, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
